  note      = {Verified via CEUR-WS volume 1133 and the paper PDF; the BX 2014 papers appear inside the EDBT/ICDT 2014 workshops volume. Builds symmetric lenses as spans of asymmetric lenses in categories that lack the required pullbacks, by finding canonical lens structures on the pullbacks of the get functions, and replaces classical span equivalence, which is too strong here, with comparison by suitably non-empty lenses. Relates the construction to the symmetric lenses of Hofmann, Pierce and Wagner.}
}

@article{johnsonrosebrughwood2012lenses,
